      "p0001-n0012-l0007"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "We constructed a mixed-effect negative binomial regression model to address the discrete nature of medal counts, effectively capturing country heterogeneity and tempo- ral unpredictability while quantifying the impact of factors like historical performance and We predicted the 2028 medal table: the United States leads with 42 gold host effects. medals(95%CI:[37,46]) and 122 total medals(95%CI:[113,131]) , followed by China with 36 gold medals([32,41]) and 91 total medals([83,100]). The 3rd to 5th places are Japan, the United Kingdom and Australia."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000017",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
